    "title": "Clubs, Free Speech, and You - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rob Lee ,\n2 hours ago In the spring of 2024, one Boston College student went “straight into a depression.” After being physically injured and arrested by a Boston police officer at a demonstration for Palestinian rights, the student—who preferred to remain anonymous due to privacy concerns—was placed on disciplinary probation by the university. “Academically, I started to sort of lose my mind,” they told me. “Emotionally, I have become very dejected and spiteful. I don’t like being on this campus, no matter how beautiful it is, just because I’m reminded of the way Boston College has failed me.” Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
